{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "05170fb6-7e1e-816c-b44b-10a0fe0318fd",
  "created_at": "2026-02-05T11:36:40-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Dennis Gallagher",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:33:54-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:33:57-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, Greg, yes, good morning. Or, it's almost noon, so, um, good morning still I guess. My name's Dennis Gallagher. I manage a property down the Point, 251 Marsh Street, and the owner, he's a nice fella, he used to run the, well, never mind that. He wants to put in a pool."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:34:14-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. An in-ground pool, above-ground?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:34:16-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Above-ground, I think. Or one of those half sunk ones? I'm not sure what you call it. Anyway, I'm looking at the television here, got it on with the sound off, some cooking competition, a fella is crying over a piece of fish. Sorry. Where was I. The pool. So there's a barrier rule, somebody told me, and I don't understand how that works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:34:36-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, pools generally have to have a barrier around them so kids can't get in. Usually a fence of a certain height with a self-closing, self-latching gate. What are you planning for the fence?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:34:47-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Chain-link. Cheapest thing, and it lasts. Whatever's allowed tall, you know, I figure go as tall as they let me. Is that, is chain-link okay for that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:34:56-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Chain-link is commonly used, yeah. The height and the details depend on the code for the pool, and I'd have the inspector go over the specifics with you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:35:05-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, the main thing, and I should've asked first, does a fence need a permit? Because my brother-in-law put one up in Middletown years ago and never got anything, but that's Middletown, and I don't know if that's, is that the same?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:35:19-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Different town, different rules. In Newport, a fence generally does need a permit, and with a pool it's going to be reviewed along with the pool permit. So you'd apply before anything goes in the ground."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:35:31-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Before. Okay. And, hang on, [pause] the guy on the TV just lost his sauce. Sorry. So the other thing, the finished side. The one side's smooth and the other's got the posts and the rails. Does the nice side have to face out? Toward the neighbors?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:35:46-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a common requirement for fences, finished side facing out. But chain-link is pretty much the same both sides, so it may not come up. I'd confirm it when you file."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:35:56-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Same both sides. Okay. So I don't need to worry. Or do I? I'm still, I'm a little mixed up on whether the pool permit and the fence permit are two separate things or one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:36:07-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Could be one application covering both, could be two forms. Easiest is to come by the office or call back with the owner's information and we'll walk you through it. Bring a sketch showing where the pool and fence go on the lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:36:21-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A sketch, okay. I can do a sketch. My handwriting's bad but I can do it. Do you need my number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:36:28-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:36:30-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0179. It's Dennis."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:36:32-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, Dennis. Stop in with the sketch and we'll sort it out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:36:37-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, thanks, Greg. I think. Thank you."
    }
  ],
